# Netlify SPA fallback. Any request that doesn't match a real file or
# directory falls through to /index.html, where React Router takes over.
# The Google OAuth callback at /login?code=... was getting Netlify's
# default 404 page because /login isn't a real file. This fixes it.
#
# Status 200 (not 301/302) means the URL bar still shows /login — React
# Router needs to see the original path, not a redirect target.
/*    /index.html    200
